Point_Camera: contiguous 15-short camera matrix (scattered-locals)

Point_Camera builds the Y-rotation camera matrix in scattered stack shorts
(local_3c pair via byte-casts, local_38..local_2c) at ebp-0x38..-0x26, multiplies it
in place twice (MulMatrix2 reads/writes 9 shorts through &local_3c) and then copies
0x1e bytes (matrix + the 12-byte trans area = a full sprite_matrix record) to
sprite_matrix. Under our compilers the scattered locals are laid out arbitrarily ->
the matrix the multiplies see is garbage -> world/sprite matrices garbage -> camera
position (ApplyMatrixLV output) garbage {0,0,huge} -> TRANSVEC.z wild -> every otz
wild -> the post-FIX-Q 0/10 OT-splice crash map. Same scattered-locals class as
patches 330/335; element mapping by ebp offset (m[0..1] = the local_3c dword pair).

